cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SimuCell3D in your research, please cite the article in
  "preferred-citation", and state the software version you used. Releases 2.x
  are maintenance releases by Nilesh Patil of the code published with the
  article; they are not reviewed or endorsed by the authors of the article,
  the Iber Lab or ETH Zurich. The release 1.0 code cited by the article is
  listed under "references".
title: SimuCell3D
type: software
abstract: >-
  SimuCell3D simulates the mechanics of three-dimensional tissues at
  subcellular resolution, with cells represented as deformable triangulated
  surfaces with polarized membranes, nuclei, extracellular matrix and lumens.
  Releases 2.x fix bugs in, add safeguards to and speed up release 1.0, the
  code published with Runser, Vetter & Iber (2024).
authors:
  - family-names: Patil
    given-names: Nilesh
version: 2.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-18'
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d"
url: "https://www.nilesh42.science/simucell3d/"
keywords:
  - tissue mechanics
  - cell-based model
  - deformable cell model
  - cell polarization
  - simulation
references:
  - type: software
    title: Source code of SimuCell3D
    authors:
      - family-names: Runser
        given-names: Steve
        affiliation: >-
          Department of Biosystems Science and Engineering (D-BSSE), ETH Zurich,
          Basel, Switzerland; Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics (SIB), Basel,
          Switzerland
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.10796908
    repository-code: "https://git.bsse.ethz.ch/iber/Publications/2024_runser_simucell3d"
    commit: 5342bf8e6e27b3b82a643fb948c4364f792da154
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >-
      Zenodo archive cited by the article (its ref. 76), published
      2024-03-08; it contains commit 5342bf8, with CONTACT_MODEL_INDEX 1 as
      the default. The tag v1.0 of this repository is the later commit
      38af451 (2024-06-26) by the same author, which adds the Fig. 1 and
      Fig. 3 input meshes and parameter files and makes CONTACT_MODEL_INDEX 2
      the default.
